WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.020
A pill taken for acne can change how a baby's face forms.

2
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.740
How can a drug for the skin reach the face?

3
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.300
Look at the hindbrain of an early embryo.

4
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.340
It shows a row of small bulges, called rhombomeres.

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.740
Early on, their cells look much alike.

6
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.440
Yet r2 will make the motor neurons that work the jaw, and r4 those that move the

7
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.760
face. Each bulge needs an address.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:31.303
The address starts with a vitamin A product, retinoic acid.

9
00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:36.883
An enzyme called Ralge II makes it in tissue beside the hindbrain and spinal cord.

10
00:00:37.523 --> 00:00:40.903
Enzymes called Cyp26 destroy it toward the front.

11
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:44.703
Think of a bath with the tap at one end and the drain at the other.

12
00:00:45.303 --> 00:00:49.863
Retinoic acid ends up high toward the back of the hindbrain and low toward the

13
00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:50.863
front.

14
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:54.573
Retinoic acid is small and oily, so it reaches the nucleus.

15
00:00:55.173 --> 00:00:57.513
There it binds a receptor called RAR.

16
00:00:58.233 --> 00:01:02.933
The receptor pairs with another one, RXR, on a short stretch of DNA.

17
00:01:03.753 --> 00:01:06.573
Hoxa1 and Hoxb1 carry such stretches.

18
00:01:07.173 --> 00:01:09.253
When the pair sits there, the gene comes on.

19
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:13.757
Hox genes sit in a row on a chromosome, and they obey a rule.

20
00:01:14.337 --> 00:01:18.917
Their order along the chromosome matches the order of their front edges along the

21
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:22.877
body. Genes at the three -prime end reach farthest forward.

22
00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:26.557
Genes toward the five -prime end stop farther back.

23
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:32.497
In cells in a dish, three -prime genes respond to lower doses of retinoic acid.

24
00:01:32.497 --> 00:01:37.997
So where the signal is lower or briefer, fewer genes come on, the three -prime ones.

25
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.980
Each rhombomere ends up with its own mix of Hox proteins.

26
00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.600
With genes like CroX -20, that mix is its address.

27
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.740
It helps decide its nerve.

28
00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.660
In the chick, r2 and r3 make the trigeminal nerve, for chewing.

29
00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.000
R4 and r5 make the facial nerve, for facial expression.

30
00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:59.273
Now change the signal.

31
00:01:59.993 --> 00:02:05.153
In mouse embryos given extra retinoic acid early, the Hox domains changed.

32
00:02:05.713 --> 00:02:10.333
Rhombomeres 2 and 3 were transformed toward the identity of 4 and 5.

33
00:02:10.813 --> 00:02:12.453
The address follows the signal.

34
00:02:12.953 --> 00:02:17.873
In early pregnancy, extra retinoic acid shifts the Hox code of the hindbrain in

35
00:02:17.873 --> 00:02:21.373
mice. That may be how a pill for the skin disturbs the face.

36
00:02:21.993 --> 00:02:24.373
Too little vitamin A harms the embryo as well.

37
00:02:24.373 --> 00:02:26.813
The dose has to be right in both directions.
